      "why": "unrolled_k is the only family in my assignment that can plausibly meet throughput >= 50 MSPS: it produces one result every ceil(N/k)+3 cycles, so it needs Fmax >= 50*(ceil(N/k)+3) MHz. With N=12..16 and k=2..4, ceil(N/k)+3 ranges from 6 (N=12,k=4) to 11 (N=16,k=2), i.e. required Fmax 300..550 MHz. The k=4, N=12 corner (300 MHz) is the most likely to be feasible in sky130. Accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is met by data_width 14..16 with n_iter 12..16 (accuracy depends only on these plus guards/rounding, identical across families). I focus the full budget here, with k biased toward 4 to hit the throughput constraint, and let Optuna trade off data_width/n_iter/guards/rounding to map the power-vs-accuracy front within the feasible region."
