  "rationale": "The binding constraint is throughput >= 50 MSPS. iterative (1 result per N+3 cycles) needs Fmax >= 50*(N+3) MHz = 650+ MHz for any N>=12, which is implausible in sky130 standard cells, so it is included only as a narrow confirmation slice with zero budget share. unrolled_k (1 result per ceil(N/k)+3 cycles) is the only family in my assignment that can plausibly meet the constraint: with k=4 and N=12 it needs only ~300 MHz. I therefore spend the entire budget on unrolled_k, restricting data_width to 14..16 and n_iter to 12..16 (the region where max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is achievable), angle_guard to -1..1 and frac_guard to 0..2 (small guards keep area/power low while preserving accuracy), rounding over both choices, and k to 2..4 (k=4 is the throughput-critical case; k=2..3 give more area/power headroom at higher Fmax). This lets Optuna map the power_index vs accuracy_bits front over the feasible region, with the selection rule (min power_index) picking the lowest-power feasible point."
